Description: Fcitx 5 mode: a second touch, the field kept in view, a readable sentence
 In Fcitx 5 mode (patch 0001) a touch on a text field that already has the
 focus shows the keyboard again: KWin 6.7.4-2+stereo3d67 says each request of
 a field on D-Bus (org.kde.kwin.VirtualKeyboard.showRequested) and the bridge
 asks KWin's own rule (willShowOnActive) as when the field gets the focus. The
 bridge tells KWin when its keyboard is shown and hidden
 (setOnScreenKeyboardShown), and KWin keeps the focused window clear of the
 keyboard's window as it does for its own panel; a KWin that cannot is said
 once in the log. The keyboard shows on the screen of the touched field: its
 layer window wants the active screen, and a keyboard already shown on another
 screen is shown again where KWin's active output is
 (org.kde.KWin.activeOutputName). "Fcitx 5 does not answer" is drawn in the
 system's negative-text colour, lightened just enough for a contrast of 4.5:1
 on the keyboard. The candidates Fcitx 5 hands over are logged in the debug
 category. Tests: testShownAgainWhenTheFieldAsks, testKWinToldWhenShown and
 testFollowsTheTouchedScreen in autotests/fcitxbridgetest.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS (row 71, second round), branch order71b of KDE's plasma/plasma-keyboard at v6.7.4
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
